  "prefLabel": "Puc 203.05 General Requirements for Written Communications",
  "priorExpiration": "2006-02-19",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 203.05 General Requirements for Written Communications. All written communications submitted to the commission shall:\n\n(a) Be dated;\n\n(b) Be signed. An electronic signature or “/s/” mark, with the full name of the signing person provided with the electronic signature or “/s/” mark, shall be an acceptable means of signing the filing;\n\n(c) Identify the name and mailing address, email address, and telephone number of the person submitting the document and the party or parties on whose behalf it is submitted, if any;\n\n(d) Identify the appropriate docket number, order number, or other pertinent subject matter;\n\n(e) Be typed on 8-1/2 by 11 inches sized paper;\n\n(f) Have no less than one-inch margins on all sides;\n\n(g) Contain sequentially numbered pages;\n\n(h) If a pleading or testimony, be double-spaced;\n\n(i) If a pleading, be filed as a separate document from any supporting materials, such as testimony and supporting attachments;\n\n(j) If materials supporting a pleading, be organized with a single series of numerical page designations, for example Bates numbering; and\n\n(k) If supporting a pleading that is over 20 pages, include a table of contents.\n\nSource. #2912, eff 11-26-84; ss by #4998, eff 11-26-90; ss by #6365, INTERIM, eff 11-18-96, EXPIRED: 3-18-97\n\nNew. #6559, eff 8-19-97, EXPIRED: 8-19-05\n\nNew. #8420, INTERIM, eff 8-23-05, EXPIRED: 2-19-06\n\nNew. #8657-A, eff 6-10-06\n\nNew. #14184, eff 1-24-25 (formerly Puc 202.06)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc200.html"
